  "live_records": {
    "q-142547": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142547",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P(Y=3\\,|\\,X=2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(Y=3\\,|\\,X=2)=\\frac{P(X=2,Y=3)}{P(X=2)}=\\frac{f(2,3)}{{f}_{X}(2)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(2) & =0.05+0.25 \\\\  & =0.30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(2,3)=0.25.$ \n\nFinally, substituting ${f}_{X}(2)=0.30$ and $f(2,3)=0.25$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=3\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{f(2,3)}{{f}_{X}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.25}{0.30} \\\\  & ≈0.83.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
