    "q-142862": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142862",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n\nCompute $P(1<Y<7\\,|\\,X=2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
      "worked_solution": "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<Y<7\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{P((1<Y<7),X=2)}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=2,(1<Y<7))}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=2,Y=3)+P(X=2,Y=5)}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2,3)+f(2,5)}{{f}_{X}(2)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(2) & =f(2,1)+f(2,3)+f(2,5)+f(2,7) \\\\  & =0+0.05+0.05+0.1 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(2,3)=0.05$ and $f(2,5)=0.05.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<Y<7\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{f(2,3)+f(2,5)}{{f}_{X}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.05+0.05}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
