    "q-142904": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142904",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n\nCompute $P(0\\le X<2\\,|\\,Y=4)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
      "worked_solution": "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X<2\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{P((0\\le X<2),Y=4)}{P(Y=4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=0,Y=4)+P(X=1,Y=4)}{P(Y=4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0,4)+f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(4) & =f(0,4)+f(1,4)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.1+0.05 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(0,4)=0.05$ and $f(1,4)=0.1.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X<2\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(0,4)+f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.05+0.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.15}{0.2} \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
