    "q-142890": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142890",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute ${f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,2)=P(X=4\\,|\\,Y=2).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=4\\,|\\,Y=2)=\\frac{P(X=4,Y=2)}{P(Y=2)}=\\frac{f(4,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(2) & =f(2,2)+f(4,2) \\\\  & =0.4+0.15 \\\\  & =0.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(4,2)=0.15.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{Y}(2)=0.55$ and $f(4,2)=0.15$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,2) & =P(X=4\\,|\\,Y=2) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.15}{0.55} \\\\  & ≈0.27.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
